WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.986
Hi! Saying Mary, Mary, Mary over and over is boring. We can use she and her instead. Today we'll learn pronouns.

2
00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:16.770
Before the verb, for the one doing the action, use I, you, he, she, it, we, they.

3
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:23.394
After a verb or a preposition, use me, you, him, her, it, us, them.

4
00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:28.290
She gave the book to him: she does the giving, and him receives it.

5
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:34.602
Tom and I is used before the verb. After it, say Tom and me.

6
00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:39.810
To show who owns something: This is my bag, or This bag is mine.

7
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.346
Also ours and theirs. No noun comes after mine.

8
00:00:44.496 --> 00:00:49.770
Reflexive pronouns are for doing something to yourself: He hurt himself.

9
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.578
For many people: ourselves, yourselves, themselves.

10
00:00:55.728 --> 00:01:01.170
Watch out! We can't use me for the person doing the action before the verb!

11
00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:06.426
Say Sam and I went to the park. It's polite to put yourself last.

12
00:01:06.576 --> 00:01:11.970
Use me after the verb: Mum took Sam and me to the park.

13
00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:21.570
Your turn! My aunt bought, ___, a toy. I, me or my? Pause and think.

14
00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:28.458
After the verb, for the person receiving it, use me. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:28.608 --> 00:01:39.858
Another one! This pencil is not mine. It is, ___. Her, hers or she? Pause and think.

16
00:01:40.008 --> 00:01:47.010
No noun follows, and it means it belongs to her, so hers. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:56.682
Here's another! The boys made the kite by, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:56.832 --> 00:02:04.290
The boys did it on their own, and boys is plural, so themselves. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:14.706
Try one more! ___, and Ravi are in the same class. I, Me or My? Pause and think.

20
00:02:14.856 --> 00:02:20.922
Before the verb, as the subject, use I. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:21.072 --> 00:02:30.906
Try one more! Grandma cut, ___, while cooking. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:31.056 --> 00:02:37.626
Grandma cut her own hand by accident, so herself. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:37.776 --> 00:02:47.682
Last one! Ravi and I lost, ___, way. Our, us or we? Pause and think.

24
00:02:47.832 --> 00:02:54.738
Ravi and I means we, and before the noun way we use our. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:54.888 --> 00:03:06.714
Remember: use I, he and she before the verb, and me, him and her after it. Use my or mine to show who owns something, and myself or himself when you do something to yourself.

26
00:03:06.864 --> 00:03:11.946
Try saying: This is my…, and This … is mine!

